 # 3\. System Modules

 The project can be divided into the following major modules.

 ### 3.1 User Authentication Module

 Responsible for:

 - User registration
- User login
- Logout
- Session management
- User profile management

---

 ### 3.2 Dashboard Module

 The dashboard provides an overview of the user's projects.

 It can display:

 - Create New Comic
- Recent Projects
- Saved Projects
- Project status
- Edit/Delete options

 Example:

```
        ComicCraft-AI
────────────────────────────
Welcome, User!

[ + Create New Comic ]

Recent Projects
────────────────────────────
My Superhero Story     [Edit]
Space Adventure        [Edit]
Mystery at School      [Edit]
```

---

 ### 3.3 Story Creation Module

 This is the primary module of the application.

 The user provides:

 - Story idea
- Genre
- Tone
- Story length
- Target audience
- Optional additional instructions

 The information is sent to the Gemini model to generate the initial story.

---

 ### 3.4 Character Creation Module

 This module generates and manages characters.

 Each character can contain:

```
Character Name
        ↓
Role
        ↓
Personality
        ↓
Appearance
        ↓
Background
        ↓
Abilities
        ↓
Relationships
```

 Users can edit or regenerate character information.

---

 ### 3.5 Scene & Dialogue Module

 The generated story is divided into scenes.

 Each scene contains:

 - Scene number
- Location
- Characters
- Actions
- Narration
- Dialogue
- Mood
- Visual description

 Gemini can generate dialogues based on the characters and scene context.

---

 ### 3.6 Comic Panel Module

 The scene is converted into individual comic panels.

 Example:

```
Scene 1
   │
   ├── Panel 1 → Establishing shot
   │
   ├── Panel 2 → Character enters
   │
   ├── Panel 3 → Character discovers object
   │
   └── Panel 4 → Character reacts
```

 Each panel can contain:

 - Panel number
- Description
- Characters
- Action
- Dialogue
- Narration
- Camera/view description
- Visual-generation prompt

---

 ### 3.7 AI Prompt Generation Module

 This module converts panel descriptions into detailed prompts suitable for a compatible image-generation system.

 Example:

```
Comic Panel:
A student discovers a glowing object inside
an old classroom.

AI Visual Prompt:
"Young student standing inside an old school
classroom, mysterious glowing blue object on
the desk, dramatic lighting, expressive face,
comic-book illustration..."
```

---

 ### 3.8 Editing Module

 Users can modify:

 - Story
- Characters
- Scenes
- Dialogues
- Panels
- Visual prompts

 The user can also request AI-based regeneration of individual sections instead of recreating the entire comic.

---

 ### 3.9 Save and Export Module

 The system stores the comic project and allows users to export the generated content.

 Possible formats include:

 - PDF
- Text
- JSON
- Structured comic document

